SUMMARY:Mac McAnally
DESCRIPTION:Record-setting 10-time CMA Musician of the Year Mac McAnally will make a stop at the Brown County Music Center in Nashville, Ind., on Friday, December 4, 2026. Mac McAnally is a Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame, Mississippi Musicians Hall of Fame and Alabama Music Hall of Fame inductee. The renowned songwriter, singer, and instrumentalist has written dozens of hit records for other artists, several of which peaked at No. 1. His own recording career began with debut hit single “It’s A Crazy World” and has grown to 14 album releases. He has written hits for Alabama, Jimmy Buffett, Kenny Chesney and Sawyer Brown, and has studio credits that include albums by Toby Keith, Linda Ronstadt, George Strait and Dolly Parton among many others.\n
