SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike Series
DESCRIPTION:Things to know for night hikes: wear close toed shoes (not sandals) and dress for the weather. Red lights are preferred for night vision and can be loaned to hikers if necessary. Please do not bring pets on night hikes. Hikers must stay with the group on night hikes.\nOgle Lake hikes use Trail 7 and are considered very rugged in the dark. Salt Creek Trail Hikes are considered moderate in the dark. Meet at the Olympic Pool for Salt Creek Hikes.\nFor questions and detailed hike information, visit the Nature Center, call 812-988-5240, email the natralist at emajor@dnr.in.gov or visit on in.gov/BrownCountySP\nSchedule:\n\nJanuary 3rd, 7pm, Ogle Lake\nJanuary 31st, 7pm, Salt Creek Trail\nFebruary 28th, 7pm, Salt Creek Trail\nApril 3rd, 8:30, Ogle Lake\nMay 1st, 9pm, Ogle Lake\nMay 30th, 9pm Salt Creek Trail\nJun 27th, 9:30pm Salt Creek Trail\nJuly 31st, 9:30pm Ogle Lake\nAugust 28th, 8:30pm Ogle Lake\nSeptember 26th, 7:30pm Salt Creek Trail\nOctober 24th, 7pm Salt Creek Trail\nDecember 23rd, 7pm Salt Creek Trail\n\n \n
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/full-moon-hike-series/
CATEGORIES:Family Friendly,Free,Happening,Outdoor Adventure,Tours
LOCATION:Brown County State Park
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Untitled-design-36.jpg
