TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Backroads Studio Tour
DESCRIPTION:Come and see live artist studios in Brown County, Indiana.\nWorking artists will welcome visitors throughout the month of October. Juried artisans, a true representation of the arts in Brown County, will share a special glimpse into the lives of working artists and craftsmen.  Don’t miss the 100th Anniversary of the Brown County Art Gallery while you’re here.\nThe Back Roads of Brown County Studio Tour is a free, self-guided event designed to showcase the arts and crafts created in the present-day “Art Colony of the Midwest.”\nWatch artwork take shape before your eyes, with artists and craftsmen demonstrating daily. Talk with artists and explore the spaces that inspire them. At some studios, you might even be able to take part in the creation in prepared activities. Educational and designed to broaden public understanding of the arts, the tour is an art celebration for the whole family.\nThis is a unique opportunity to meet artists doing what they love and to purchase artwork directly from those who made it. Collectors will relish the selection of new work made available especially for this event.\nAll studios are open Wednesday – Saturday 10:00am – 5:00pm daily in October. Many studios are open Sunday 10:00 am – 5:00 pm. Check the artist listing here ( https://bcstudiotour.com/artists/ ) for hours for each studio.\nMost studios take credit card payments, but some do not, often because of limited internet service in backroads art studios. So, bring your checkbook or some extra cash along, just in case!\n
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/backroads-studio-tour/
CATEGORIES:Art Events &amp; Exhibits,Classes &amp; Workshops,Fall,Family Friendly,Free,Happening,Special Events,Tours
LOCATION:Brown County
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/BVB-Outdoors-Fall-Country-Road-Orange_CHP-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
